{
  "about": "docs/api/thread-search-v1.md, 'The vectors of the corpus'. One person's threads, in the order of their ids (a newer thread has a greater id). `events` are the events of the log that matter to search: `user_message` and `agent_message` (`text`, `messageId`, `final`, `purpose`); the others carry nothing searched. `archived` is whether the person archived the thread, `edit` whether it was made by an edit of a message (a branch), `copiedThrough` is the seq of the last event copied from a parent that still exists (absent: the thread has no parent, or its parent is gone); `parent` names that parent (absent: the thread of id ...0003), whose first `copiedThrough` events are the fork's. A text is a string or `{repeat, times, suffix?}`. `queries/*.json` ask this corpus.",
